{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/31510-empire-city-by-night-an-online-chronicle-for-classic-world-of-darkness","id":31510,"title":"Empire City by Night: An Online Chronicle for Classic World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-16T23:47:32-08:00","id":31510,"title":"Empire City by Night: An Online Chronicle for Classic World of Darkness","content":"Hey guys, I am in the early planning stages of creating an online chronicle for Classic World of Darkness (with some homebrew tweaks to the fluff) which will be held either on Skype (where we will follow the Vampire venues) or as a forum-based game where we will follow multiple venues.<br /> <br /> The game is set in the fictional Empire City, a large American metropolis on the East Coast, based on elements from multiple cities all over the United States. It is set in what is nominally the Classic World of Darkness, but with some heavy tweaks.<br /> <br /> First off, the Revised metaplot did not happen at all. So, Gangrel are still in the Camarilla, there was no Week of Nightmares, no Red Star, no Avatar Storm, no Sixth Great Maelstrom. As such, we will use 20th Anniversary rules for Vampire, Werewolf, and Mortals, and 2nd Edition for Mages.<br /> <br /> Second, the games Kindred of the East and Demon: The Fallen are NOT canon in this version of the World of Darkness, There are no Fallen and no Kuei-Jin. East Asia's cities are dominated by traditional Cainite vampires, but the Camarilla and Sabbat have almost no sway in Asia, instead the vampires of Asia rule with their own courts in a Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom style situation.<br /> <br /> Because of the metaplot being negated, Hunter: The Reckoning didn't happen either.<br /> <br /> The Classic World of Darkness fan-game <b>Senshi: The Merchandising, </b>(I hope discussing fan-games aren't against the rules), a humorous yet awesome fan game whose rules can be found on the fan-game's webpage (a quick Google search should pull it up on the first page), IS part of the canon of Empire City by Night, if only because I enjoy it so much.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will let people vote on whether or not we will use the setting of Empire Bay as a singular Vampire game over Skype, or as a multi-venue game in forum format.<br /> <br /> If we go with the Forums format, then the following venues are in play. I can be the Storyteller for Vampire, Senshi, and Mortals, but I need help for Werewolf and Mage.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Masquerade </b>(20th Anniversary Edition)<br /> <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse </b>(20th Anniversary Edition)<br /> <b>Mage: The Ascension </b>(2nd Edition, at least until I can acquire M20)<br /> <b>Mortals </b>(V20 rules, with material derived from all three editions. Hunters, Kinfolk, and Ghouls, all fall in this category)<br /> <b>Senshi: The Merchandising </b>(Fan-made Game, uses Revised rules)<br /> <br /> <b>Wraith: The Oblivion, Changeling: The Dreaming, </b>and <b>Mummy: The Resurrection </b>are canon in a broad strokes way, but are not playable venues unless there is enough demand for these venues and someone who can ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's what I have laid down for each venue. Senshi: The Merchandising doesn't really need any rules or guidelines laid down since anything in the webpage's rules is fair game and there isn't much to expand on beyond the core rules and the sole splatbook on the Sailor Scouts.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b><br /> All thirteen main clans are in play, as are all four major sects (Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, and Independents). Bloodlines and minor sects (Children of Osiris, Inconnu, Black Hand, and Tal'Ma'he Ra) are all canonically in existence, but not playable.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b><br /> The main tribes of the Garou Nation (including the Stargazers) are all playable. Other Fera may become playable if we get enough players and an ST willing to handle Fera.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage: The Ascension</b><br /> The Traditions are the only groups in play for Mage, but once again, if there is enough demand and an appropriate ST, the Technocracy will become playable as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Mortals</b><br /> Hunters, Ghouls, Kinfolk, and regular humans will all be playable. The following Hunter organizations are in play: <i>The Society of Leopold, The Arcanum, FBI Special Affairs Department, NSA, The Shih, Strike Force Zero, Pentex, The Young Bloods. </i>We will use material found in <i><b>The Hunters Hunted, The Inquisition, Project Twilight, Halls of the Arcanum, Demon Hunter X, World of Darkness: Mafia, Ghouls: Fatal Addiction, Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, </b></i>and <b><i>The Hunters Hunted II.</i></b> Gypsies will not be playable for rather obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, is anyone interested in this game, either as a V20 game over Skype or a multi-venue forum game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T01:37:36-08:00","id":31545,"title":"","content":"Definitely interested in some mage, however that goes about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T06:03:18-08